1
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,600
Why won't you accept
that I'm trying to help?

2
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:11,880
I don't have a father.

3
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,120
If you want me to bow to you that badly…

4
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,040
Kill him.

5
00:03:14,120 --> 00:03:17,040
…I'll do it at your funeral.

6
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,520
‎PREVIOUSLY

7
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:19,520
I forgive you.

8
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:23,160
Ramil inherited everything
from his father.

9
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,360
We don't have to struggle anymore.

10
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,800
Then go with him.

11
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,480
Maybe he'll finally stop barking.

12
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:37,160
This is the worst day of my life, Mom.

13
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,280
Ramil.

14
00:03:54,240 --> 00:03:57,480
I'm glad your father is dead.

15
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,600
How can you say that?

16
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:05,880
I thought you'd be happy your father died.

17
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,320
You inherited everything

18
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,840
and became rich overnight.

19
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:14,040
Now that you're rich,

20
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:15,960
why put up with living here?

21
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:19,800
Get out. And take your wife with you.

22
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:21,519
I'm sick of looking at both of you.

23
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,800
I'm not leaving.

24
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,520
I'm staying here.

25
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,480
What are you staying for?

26
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,640
Mom.

27
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,480
They're parasites by nature.

28
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,600
They're so used to clinging
to other people.

29
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,680
They need a collar

30
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:46,400
and someone constantly yanking the leash.

31
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:48,560
They can't live on their own.

32
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:54,800
Ramil chose to stay here because
he wants to help finish Grandpa's work.

33
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:59,440
That's right. I could go back
and work for my father's company now.

34
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:01,920
But I'm staying here

35
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,800
until I finish Mr. Pichai's work.
Then I'll leave.

36
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:07,960
-You don't have to--
-Fine.

37
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,840
Go back to doing your job.

38
00:05:11,880 --> 00:05:14,840
But you better
earn your keep in this house.

39
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,800
Miss Hathaya, the hospital
just brought Mr. Pichai home.

40
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,080
Okay, Aunt Ann.

41
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,800
Let's go see Grandpa.

42
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,880
You shouldn't have
let him get involved again.

43
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:49,360
Raiwin asked me to, Mom.

44
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:51,480
Ramil inherited a lot of money.

45
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,520
We need to be nice to him now.

46
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:56,000
Maybe we can get something out of him.

47
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,000
Madam.

48
00:06:02,400 --> 00:06:06,600
Mr. Pichai is back. Aren't you afraid
he'll tell everyone the truth?

49
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:11,280
Grandpa is basically unresponsive.
I'm not afraid of him.

50
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,040
You're the one

51
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,160
who needs to zip it.

52
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,680
If you tell anyone…

53
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,800
I'll kill you.

54
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:27,320
Yes. I'll seal my mouth shut with cement.

55
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:48,200
Grandpa, you're home now.

56
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,600
Ramil and I will take care of you.

57
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,720
You have to stay strong.

58
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:04,040
Soon you'll be able
to talk and walk again.

59
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:10,120
I'll take the best
possible care of you, sir.

60
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:14,440
The development is almost finished too.

61
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:17,600
We're waiting for you to come inspect it.

62
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:29,480
You two can go to work now.

63
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,200
Grandpa just got home.

64
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:40,200
I want to take the day off
to look after him.

65
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,880
Go to work, Hathaya.

66
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:46,520
Mom and I will take care of Grandpa here.

67
00:07:49,360 --> 00:07:50,280
Go.

68
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,760
I'm his daughter-in-law,

69
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:56,720
and Chayanee is his beloved granddaughter.
We'll take care of him.

70
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:06,360
Aunt Ann, please take care of him.

71
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:07,680
Of course.

72
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:35,440
I really don't want to leave.
I'm worried about Grandpa.

73
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:39,760
It's okay. Aunt Ann
is taking care of him. Don't worry.

74
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,760
We need to finish the work

75
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:46,640
so Grandpa will be happy. Okay?

76
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,160
You can leave now.

77
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:59,240
I'm staying to take care of him.

78
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:02,000
My daughter and I will stay with Father.

79
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:06,240
But Miss Hathaya told me
not to leave his side.

80
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:09,840
How dare you? Who pays your salary?

81
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,720
Talk back to me one more time

82
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:15,160
and I'll fire you.
Go make Father some food.

83
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,880
-Chamoi.
-Yes?

84
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:29,560
Stand guard. Don't let her
stick her nose in here right now.

85
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:30,760
Yes, madam.

86
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,760
Grandpa.

87
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,320
I'm sorry.

88
00:09:46,320 --> 00:09:48,960
I didn't mean to hurt you.

89
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:54,160
I'll make up for what I did
by taking care of you.

90
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,400
I won't hurt you.

91
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:04,360
I want you to see me succeed.

92
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,760
Soon…

93
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:13,960
you'll see that
this granddaughter you love

94
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:19,400
is a thousand times better
than that parasite.

95
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,360
Father.

96
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:28,400
Stay with us long enough
to see your granddaughter succeed.

97
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,080
-Papang.
-Daddy!

98
00:10:41,160 --> 00:10:43,440
Papang. Papang.

99
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:52,320
I missed you to the moon and back, Daddy.

100
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:56,720
I missed you too.
But what does that even mean?

101
00:10:56,800 --> 00:11:00,440
I mean more than anything in the world.

102
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:04,640
Papang, who brought you here?

103
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:07,640
-Mommy.
-Mommy?

104
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:10,680
Where is she? Did she already leave?

105
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:13,680
Mommy is taking care
of Great-Grandpa Pichai.

106
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:14,960
What?

107
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:24,040
You're back?

108
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:28,240
I'll take over with Grandpa now.
Thank you.

109
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:30,880
It's fine. I can take care of him.

110
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:34,040
I used to look after my own grandfather
when he was bedridden.

111
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:36,640
It would be better to let
his granddaughter care for him.

112
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:42,680
As for you, come talk to me.

113
00:11:47,240 --> 00:11:48,400
Papang.

114
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:52,240
Go read Great-Grandpa a story, okay?

115
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,640
Okay.

116
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,880
Come on.

117
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,160
You brought Papang here. Now you can go.

118
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:08,320
I'll take care of him.
How many days will you be working?

119
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:11,880
-When are you coming back to get him?
-I'm not going anywhere.

120
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,840
I brought him here
because we're both staying.

121
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:16,160
No.

122
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:20,080
Think about it carefully.

123
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,240
If you and Hathaya go to work,

124
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:26,040
are you really going to leave
Mr. Pichai with the maids all day?

125
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:28,000
I don't think that's appropriate.

126
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:30,760
I can volunteer
to take care of him myself.

127
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,120
And I think

128
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:37,080
a child in the house might
make Mr. Pichai happier too.

129
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,520
Papang loves talking and asking questions.

130
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:44,080
That can help stimulate his awareness.

131
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:46,960
Even if he can't respond verbally,

132
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,960
he can still understand through feelings.

133
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:52,360
It may help improve
his emotional well-being.

134
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:55,160
And I think

135
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:58,920
before long, Mr. Pichai
will be able to talk and walk again.

136
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,400
Thanks for the advice.

137
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:06,280
But no. I can figure something out myself.
I don't need to depend on you.

138
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,800
Why?

139
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:12,840
Do you hate me?
Or are you afraid you'll lose?

140
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:17,040
Afraid you'll give in
to your own feelings?

141
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:19,760
I already told you.

142
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,600
I'm only being Papang's father.

143
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:25,000
I've never had feelings for you.

144
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:28,400
You won't give me even one chance?

145
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,640
Let Nuchwara stay here.

146
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:39,040
I don't want Papang separated from
his mother. Plus, he's good for Grandpa.

147
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,480
Accept Nuchwara's offer.

148
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:50,200
Even if I agree,
the owners of the house won't.

149
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:54,000
I'll talk to Aunt Liu and Chayanee myself.

150
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:56,640
I'm going to stay with my son.

151
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:08,600
What are you doing?

152
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:11,600
You know Liu and Chayanee
will never agree to this.

153
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:12,960
I know.

154
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:15,800
Then why would you do it?

155
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,800
I have my own way.

156
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:22,720
I'm surprised you asked
to meet me privately.

157
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:25,560
This must be something big and important.

158
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:27,800
It is.

159
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:30,960
It's very important for Grandpa.

160
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:33,680
If it matters that much to you,

161
00:14:33,760 --> 00:14:37,400
I'm happy to help. What do you need?

162
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,000
Well…

163
00:14:41,040 --> 00:14:45,240
I want you to talk to Chayanee for me.

164
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:47,640
Ask her

165
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:52,000
to let Nuchwara and Papang
stay at the house.

166
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:01,280
I can't help you with that.

167
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:06,000
I know it makes you uncomfortable,

168
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:10,160
but Chayanee only listens to you.

169
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,080
And

170
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,920
you once told Ramil

171
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:20,000
that you wanted to prove you were sincere.

172
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:23,160
This could be a good opportunity.

173
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,160
If you help,

174
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:28,640
I think Ramil may finally forgive you.

175
00:15:29,520 --> 00:15:31,560
You shouldn't have asked him for help.

176
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:36,480
I had to. I want Grandpa
to recover as quickly as possible.

177
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,840
And I'm also doing this for Papang.

178
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:40,920
What's Papang to do with it?

179
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:45,800
I want to use this opportunity to let
Raiwin and Papang spend time together.

180
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,840
Are you going to reveal
that they're father and son?

181
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,640
I just want Raiwin to accept the truth

182
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,720
and take responsibility for Papang.

183
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:58,920
But if he still refuses,
I won't demand anything.

184
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:03,640
I just want father and son to have
a chance to be close to each other.

185
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:07,040
Did he agree to help?

186
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:09,760
I'm not sure.

187
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,280
Miss Hathaya.

188
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:18,880
Madam Liu and Miss Chayanee are back.
Something terrible is happening.

189
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:26,200
Get out of this house. Get out!

190
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:31,280
Papang, say hello to Grandma and Auntie.

191
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:34,320
Hello, Grandma. Hello, Auntie.

192
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,600
Don't say hello to me.

193
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:40,440
-Get out.
-I'm not related to either of you.

194
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:43,120
Get the hell out of my house right now.

195
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:48,640
It's okay. Don't be scared, sweetheart.

196
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,040
Papang, remember this.

197
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:57,000
Shouting at people like this is very rude

198
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:59,360
and aggressive.

199
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:01,560
If you behaved this badly,

200
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,000
nobody would want to be your friend.

201
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,280
People would say your parents
never taught you any manners.

202
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:11,319
Madam, she's insulting you
without saying it directly.

203
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:15,520
Why are you standing there like an idiot?
Drag them out of my house right now.

204
00:17:15,599 --> 00:17:18,920
-Get out. Come on.
-Don't touch me.

205
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,240
I said get out. Come on.

206
00:17:21,319 --> 00:17:23,480
-Right now.
-Don't touch my son.

207
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,680
Let go of him.

208
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,960
-Give me the kid.
-Let go.

209
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:32,520
I said let go.

210
00:17:33,640 --> 00:17:34,920
You're hurting me.

211
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,520
-Let go of my son right now.
-Okay!

212
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,280
Shut up!

213
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:41,240
Your mother insulted me

214
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:44,440
and my mother. She did something wrong,

215
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:48,080
so she needs to be punished.
But I don't feel like punishing you.

216
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:50,160
I'd rather punish your son.

217
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,040
-Come here.
-Don't touch my son. Let go.

218
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:59,360
-Get out of here.
-Don't touch my son. Let go.

219
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:02,120
-Stop! Don't. I said stop.
-Stay back!

220
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:06,200
Why did you get involved?

221
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,800
Papang is my son.

222
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:10,600
If you hurt him,
I'll make sure you answer for it.

223
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:12,080
You think I'm scared of you?

224
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:16,160
Have you forgotten that my daughter
and I are in charge of this house?

225
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:19,280
Aunt Liu, please.

226
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:22,360
I'm the one who asked Nuchwara
and Papang to stay here.

227
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:26,080
And what gives you the right to invite
anyone you want into this house?

228
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:28,680
You think this is some kind of shelter?

229
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,680
Get out.

230
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,480
-Aunt Chamoi.
-Yes, Miss Chayanee.

231
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:38,320
Call the police and have them
drag all of them out.

232
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,760
Of course. I'll call 1669.

233
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:44,880
You idiot. Are you trying to call
an ambulance to collect your own body?

234
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,160
Dial 191.

235
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:50,000
Right. I'll call the whole
police station if I have to.

236
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:53,400
Please don't call them.

237
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:02,400
I'd like Nuchwara
and her son to stay here.

238
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:04,960
Why do you want her to stay here?

239
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:08,600
I know you love Grandpa
and worry about him.

240
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:13,640
Nuchwara is experienced in caring
for bedridden patients. She could help.

241
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:16,360
We don't need that woman.

242
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:21,200
Chayanee and I were already
planning to hire a nurse for Father.

243
00:19:21,280 --> 00:19:22,440
Aunt Liu,

244
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:26,400
Nuchwara really does have experience
caring for bedridden patients.

245
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:29,240
And Mr. Pichai loves Papang.

246
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:32,880
Having Papang around will make him happy.
That can help his health too.

247
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:38,000
-But I think--
-Please.

248
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,200
Please, honey.

249
00:19:49,080 --> 00:19:50,600
Please.

250
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,360
Fine. I'll agree.

251
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,400
But you have to do something for me.

252
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:06,400
Anything. What do you want?

253
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:12,160
You have to move in here with me.

254
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,760
Well?

255
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:35,520
If you don't move in here with me,

256
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:38,560
I'm throwing them out.

257
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:52,680
I already want to be with you.

258
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:56,960
Once Mr. Pichai gets better, I'll have
my father arrange the wedding.

259
00:20:58,600 --> 00:20:59,880
You said it.

260
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:18,800
What are you all standing
around for? Hathaya.

261
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:20,840
Take them to the workers' quarters.

262
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:25,080
Come on, Papang. Come with Daddy.

263
00:21:27,920 --> 00:21:31,200
Chayanee, sweetheart. Tone it down.

264
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:41,760
I'm going now, Mom.

265
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:42,960
Chayanee, sweetheart.

266
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:46,200
Don't lose yourself over a man.

267
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,040
You'll end up in trouble.

268
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:50,400
That's right, Miss Chayanee.

269
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:53,680
Giving in to a man too much
can ruin your life.

270
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,480
I've seen it happen plenty of times.

271
00:21:57,280 --> 00:22:01,880
Aunt Chamoi, the man you're
talking about is my husband-to-be.

272
00:22:04,920 --> 00:22:06,200
-I'm off, Mom.
-All right.

273
00:22:08,560 --> 00:22:10,720
-Ready to go?
-Yes.

274
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:45,760
Where are you going?

275
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:47,760
Where's Chayanee's room?

276
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:49,920
What are you planning?

277
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:53,640
I'm bringing food.

278
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:58,720
If I were the boss
and had a stupid maid like you,

279
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:02,640
I would've fired you long ago.
Did you forget

280
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:05,080
Raiwin is staying with Miss Chayanee?

281
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:08,480
Go make another serving.
I didn't make this for your boss.

282
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:10,200
I made it for Raiwin alone.

283
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:12,040
What are you thinking?

284
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,640
Trying to steal the boss's husband

285
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:16,880
so you can be
the subdistrict chief's wife?

286
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,880
-Think whatever you want.
-Stop at once.

287
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:22,360
Mr. Raiwin loves Miss Chayanee very much.

288
00:23:22,440 --> 00:23:25,080
He would never look twice
at someone like you.

289
00:23:25,160 --> 00:23:26,240
Give this to Raiwin.

290
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:28,360
Who do you think you are?

291
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:31,160
You keep calling him by his first name.
Call him Mr. Raiwin.

292
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:34,240
Give this to Raiwin for me.

293
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:38,360
Mr. Raiwin isn't here.
He already left for work.

294
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:41,800
Where are you taking that?

295
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:45,520
I didn't bring it for your boss.
If Raiwin isn't here,

296
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:47,920
I'll feed it to the dog.

297
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,560
Oh my God.

298
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:52,480
Madam!

299
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:04,360
What do you want for lunch?
I'll go get it.

300
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:06,760
Anything is fine.

301
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:10,040
That is really broad.

302
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:14,200
Can you narrow it down? Rice or noodles?

303
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:17,600
I'm tired of rice. And noodles

304
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:19,000
never fill me up.

305
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:21,040
Then what do you want?

306
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:23,680
Can I eat you?

307
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:30,000
I'm kidding.

308
00:24:30,720 --> 00:24:33,600
Don't look at me like that.

309
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:36,440
Let's get something
from the place by the entrance.

310
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:38,640
Made-to-order food. Let's go.

311
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:41,120
I already made food for everyone.

312
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:44,640
Plenty of food, boss.

313
00:24:45,480 --> 00:24:48,440
You really didn't have to make all this.
I can buy food myself.

314
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:52,320
Food from outside
is hard to trust these days.

315
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:54,200
Veggies are sprayed with chemicals.

316
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:58,400
I made this myself, so I know it's safe.

317
00:24:58,480 --> 00:25:01,160
These are all your favorites.

318
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:06,600
Try this. I'll feed you.

319
00:25:06,680 --> 00:25:08,880
It's okay. I can eat by myself.

320
00:25:14,120 --> 00:25:17,080
Tofu. Good protein.

321
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:21,840
Easy to digest.

322
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:24,720
Here. Let me feed you.

323
00:25:25,320 --> 00:25:28,960
No, it's okay, Nuch. I can eat by myself.

324
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:33,480
Eat some fish.

325
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:36,480
Maybe it'll make you smarter.

326
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:48,480
Want some egg? A nice big one.

327
00:26:12,560 --> 00:26:13,520
Have some soup.

328
00:26:15,080 --> 00:26:16,720
So you don't choke.

329
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:37,840
My plate is already full.

330
00:26:37,920 --> 00:26:39,800
I don't think I can keep up.

331
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:41,960
Actually,

332
00:26:42,480 --> 00:26:44,520
I should go to the bathroom.

333
00:26:44,600 --> 00:26:47,720
Max. Didn't you say you had to pee?

334
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:48,680
Let's go together.

335
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:50,920
When did I say that?

336
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:53,520
Just now. You forgot already?

337
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:55,680
You said you had to pee. Let's go.

338
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:57,880
-Come on.
-Right.

339
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,360
I really have to go.

340
00:26:59,440 --> 00:27:01,920
Where's the bathroom, boss?

341
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:08,360
What do you want?

342
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:11,320
Ramil. That's what I want.

343
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:14,000
He may be the man you love,

344
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:17,520
but you're not the woman he loves.

345
00:27:17,600 --> 00:27:20,880
Are you a psychic?
How do you know how he feels?

346
00:27:21,400 --> 00:27:23,360
I've been with him a long time.

347
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:27,520
We're together every day. I know him well.

348
00:27:29,160 --> 00:27:32,880
Let's not argue
over something so pointless.

349
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:35,680
Who knows him better doesn't matter.

350
00:27:36,600 --> 00:27:40,640
What matters is who his heart belongs to.

351
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:48,640
War is about to break out, boss.

352
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:51,320
You're exaggerating.

353
00:27:52,120 --> 00:27:53,080
Then,

354
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:57,480
why don't you pick a side
before the war starts?

355
00:27:58,960 --> 00:27:59,920
I'm not choosing.

356
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:04,800
What? Why not? Are you choosing violence?

357
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,200
I want to know for sure

358
00:28:07,280 --> 00:28:09,560
if Hathaya is only protecting me

359
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,040
or if she really has feelings.

360
00:28:16,600 --> 00:28:18,200
Are you planning to compete with me?

361
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:23,720
I'm not trying to compete.
I'm protecting him.

362
00:28:24,320 --> 00:28:26,840
I'm not going to let you hurt him again.

363
00:28:27,360 --> 00:28:29,960
That isn't your responsibility.

364
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:33,440
He doesn't belong to you.

365
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:38,560
What if I want him to?

366
00:28:42,120 --> 00:28:46,080
Then I guess you and I
will have to fight for him.

367
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:55,560
Aren't you eating? There's plenty left.
You barely ate anything earlier.

368
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:01,880
I don't share with others.

369
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:16,440
I'm here to see the chief. Is he here?

370
00:29:17,040 --> 00:29:18,920
He went out to inspect some work.

371
00:29:19,680 --> 00:29:22,960
You're lying. I saw
Raiwin's car parked outside.

372
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:26,240
The Chief took an official vehicle today.

373
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:29,120
I'll wait in his office.

374
00:29:29,840 --> 00:29:32,840
Then please wait in the reception room.

375
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:34,160
I'll bring you some coffee.

376
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:36,680
I'm waiting in Raiwin's office.

377
00:29:42,080 --> 00:29:42,960
What happened?

378
00:29:43,560 --> 00:29:45,080
A showdown is about to happen.

379
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:49,000
Another woman came earlier,
claiming she was close to the chief.

380
00:29:49,080 --> 00:29:50,080
She's waiting in there.

381
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:55,120
No wonder the locals say
the chief's girlfriend is crazy jealous.

382
00:29:55,200 --> 00:29:57,400
She attacks any woman who gets near him.

383
00:29:57,480 --> 00:30:00,720
What do we do?

384
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:03,120
Call the chief to come back now.

385
00:30:12,040 --> 00:30:13,360
What are you doing in here?

386
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:18,120
Open your eyes and look.

387
00:30:19,440 --> 00:30:21,160
This is my boyfriend's office.

388
00:30:21,240 --> 00:30:22,680
Get out.

389
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:29,720
Is there some rule saying
a citizen isn't allowed

390
00:30:29,800 --> 00:30:31,520
to bring flowers to the chief?

391
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:35,200
I just wanted to thank him
for working so hard for the people,

392
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:37,040
so I brought some flowers. That's all.

393
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:44,080
Flowers?

394
00:30:48,280 --> 00:30:49,680
What kind of flowers?

395
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:54,640
Roses…

396
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:58,000
don't suit you.

397
00:30:58,520 --> 00:31:02,720
You're just cheap trash.

398
00:31:05,120 --> 00:31:06,720
Then what flower suits you?

399
00:31:08,960 --> 00:31:10,200
Me?

400
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:15,400
Sweet peas suit me well,
since I'm Raiwin's sweetheart.

401
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,760
What are you laughing at?

402
00:31:25,640 --> 00:31:28,160
I'm laughing because of your comparison.

403
00:31:30,600 --> 00:31:31,680
The only flower

404
00:31:32,400 --> 00:31:36,000
that really suits you
is one from the thorn trees in hell.

405
00:31:37,160 --> 00:31:39,320
How dare you insult me?

406
00:31:40,040 --> 00:31:41,920
You're climbing a thorn tree for adultery.

407
00:31:42,560 --> 00:31:44,480
You're the other woman.
Didn't you realize?

408
00:31:44,560 --> 00:31:48,600
What the hell are you talking about?
Get out. Get out right now.

409
00:31:51,760 --> 00:31:52,840
I said get out.

410
00:31:56,680 --> 00:31:57,640
You're not leaving?

411
00:31:58,760 --> 00:31:59,680
What happened?

412
00:31:59,760 --> 00:32:03,480
Chief, hurry and stop them.
They're yelling so loudly in your office.

413
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:06,760
With that much noise,
they're definitely fighting.

414
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:11,320
Fine. I'll drag you out myself.

415
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:12,280
Go.

416
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:16,680
Take your bag too. Get out. Go.

417
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:19,120
Help! Help me!

418
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:21,520
-Someone help!
-Stop.

419
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:24,480
Chayanee. Let go. Let her go.

420
00:32:27,120 --> 00:32:28,920
Chayanee…

421
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:32,680
Chayanee is hurting me.

422
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:39,720
You lying bitch.

423
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:44,160
I'll slap you to death myself.

424
00:32:45,120 --> 00:32:48,520
Chayanee. Enough. Stop.

425
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:54,640
You pushed me? And you're protecting her?

426
00:32:56,240 --> 00:32:57,400
Get a grip.

427
00:32:58,320 --> 00:33:01,080
Do you even realize what you're doing?

428
00:33:01,160 --> 00:33:02,640
She came into your office

429
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:05,160
trying to seduce you. Can't you see that?

430
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,160
That's not true.

431
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:15,960
I only wanted to encourage you

432
00:33:16,040 --> 00:33:18,600
because I've seen how hard
you work for the people.

433
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:23,520
So I came to arrange
some flowers for you. But…

434
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,840
Chayanee misunderstood
and thought I was trying to seduce you.

435
00:33:30,960 --> 00:33:32,440
So she…

436
00:33:34,480 --> 00:33:35,560
slapped me…

437
00:33:37,440 --> 00:33:38,640
pulled my hair…

438
00:33:40,240 --> 00:33:42,240
and threw flowers at me.

439
00:33:47,040 --> 00:33:47,920
You lying bitch.

440
00:33:50,560 --> 00:33:51,400
That's not true.

441
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:55,200
She started it.

442
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:56,640
She insulted me.

443
00:33:56,720 --> 00:33:59,280
She called me an adulteress
who belongs on the thorn tree.

444
00:33:59,360 --> 00:34:01,680
She was saying all kinds
of crazy things about me.

445
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:04,680
What exactly did you mean by that?

446
00:34:04,760 --> 00:34:09,560
Tell everyone why you called me

447
00:34:09,639 --> 00:34:11,719
an adulteress. Say it.

448
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:24,120
I think this is all a misunderstanding.

449
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:27,440
Let's end it here.

450
00:34:29,520 --> 00:34:32,080
Nuch, go home.

451
00:34:32,159 --> 00:34:33,400
Okay.

452
00:34:34,520 --> 00:34:36,120
I won't bother you again.

453
00:34:37,199 --> 00:34:38,719
I don't want to cause you trouble.

454
00:34:46,360 --> 00:34:48,040
I think

455
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:50,800
you misunderstood me.

456
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:55,159
So,

457
00:34:56,040 --> 00:34:57,520
let's just end this here.

458
00:35:15,040 --> 00:35:18,120
This is only the beginning.
See you in round two.

459
00:35:21,640 --> 00:35:24,840
-You!
-Hey! Let her go.

460
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:27,320
-Let her go.
-You lying bitch!

461
00:35:27,400 --> 00:35:29,640
Enough. Let her go.

462
00:35:29,720 --> 00:35:32,560
-Let her go. Go, Nuch.
-Let go.

463
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:35,160
Chayanee. Enough.

464
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,360
Enough.

465
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:40,080
We're going home.

466
00:35:40,160 --> 00:35:42,440
-Come on.
-Let go.

467
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,440
Delete that video.

468
00:35:44,520 --> 00:35:46,440
This was just a misunderstanding.

469
00:35:46,960 --> 00:35:48,240
Come on. Let's go home.

470
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:50,440
We're going home now.

471
00:35:54,840 --> 00:35:56,640
The chief wants us to delete the video.

472
00:35:57,560 --> 00:36:01,400
What a shame. If we posted this,
it would break the internet.

473
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:06,120
You're the only one
who agreed to delete it. I didn't.

474
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:09,200
Don't you feel sorry for the chief?

475
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:14,560
No. His father was already trying
to pocket kickbacks before him.

476
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:18,000
People like this need to learn a lesson.

477
00:36:40,520 --> 00:36:46,600
Little cuckoo bird

478
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:53,320
You left your egg for Mother Crow to hatch

479
00:36:54,560 --> 00:36:59,440
Mother Crow grew to love it

480
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:05,720
Thinking it was her own child

481
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:11,040
She brought rice and food

482
00:37:12,160 --> 00:37:15,880
Fed it and cared for it

483
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:21,480
Kept it safe inside the nest

484
00:37:23,520 --> 00:37:28,120
And always brought it something to eat

485
00:37:33,440 --> 00:37:35,360
You sang him

486
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:37,640
right into a good dream.

487
00:37:40,640 --> 00:37:44,120
Why do you always sing

488
00:37:44,920 --> 00:37:47,000
that cuckoo lullaby to him?

489
00:37:48,680 --> 00:37:49,880
When I was little,

490
00:37:51,640 --> 00:37:53,600
Grandpa used to sing it to me.

491
00:37:54,600 --> 00:37:56,920
So I've known it since I was a child.

492
00:37:57,880 --> 00:38:00,120
And I like what it means.

493
00:38:02,200 --> 00:38:03,760
This song

494
00:38:04,680 --> 00:38:07,440
speaks for a lot of people.

495
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:12,560
Even when people aren't family by blood,

496
00:38:14,640 --> 00:38:16,920
love and the bond between them

497
00:38:18,240 --> 00:38:20,240
can still make them family.

498
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:31,600
Aunt Ann, is Daddy back?

499
00:38:31,680 --> 00:38:34,600
-Where is he?
-In Grandpa's room.

500
00:38:34,680 --> 00:38:37,840
I'm going to read a story
to him and Daddy.

501
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:40,920
That's sweet.

502
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,680
I like

503
00:38:48,560 --> 00:38:49,600
that cuckoo lullaby.

504
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:52,560
It makes me think

505
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,400
of Papang and me.

506
00:38:57,080 --> 00:38:58,920
I agreed to be Papang's father.

507
00:39:00,240 --> 00:39:01,640
I've raised him for so long…

508
00:39:03,320 --> 00:39:04,800
that I truly feel…

509
00:39:06,400 --> 00:39:08,320
like I'm his real father.

510
00:39:09,680 --> 00:39:13,960
If someone tried to take Papang
away from me now, I wouldn't allow it.

511
00:39:16,640 --> 00:39:19,280
I'll help you take care of Papang
and protect him too.

512
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:22,040
Thank you.

513
00:39:26,840 --> 00:39:27,960
Papang.

514
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:32,200
Papang.

515
00:39:32,280 --> 00:39:34,240
How long have you been standing there?

516
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:39,320
I just got here.

517
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:46,680
I'm going to read Great-Grandpa a story.

518
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:19,240
Madam. Madam. Miss Chayanee is famous now.

519
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:23,880
Really? Was she interviewed on the news?
Let me see.

520
00:40:23,960 --> 00:40:27,960
No. Someone posted a video
of Miss Chayanee and Nuchwara fighting

521
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:29,960
at the Subdistrict Office.
It's going viral.

522
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:34,080
Delete it. Go after every copy
and get them all taken down.

523
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:37,160
-Quickly.
-There's no way to delete all of them.

524
00:40:37,240 --> 00:40:38,800
It's all over the internet.

525
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:40,520
Delete everything.

526
00:40:40,600 --> 00:40:43,920
Chayanee. Stop right now.
We need to settle this.

527
00:40:46,160 --> 00:40:50,160
Do you realize what you've done? I told
you not to go to the Subdistrict Office.

528
00:40:50,240 --> 00:40:53,840
You keep yelling at me. Why don't you
tell Nuchwara to stay away instead?

529
00:40:53,920 --> 00:40:55,480
Why do you care so much about her

530
00:40:55,560 --> 00:40:58,640
and treat her with so much respect
when she's just Ramil's wife?

531
00:40:58,720 --> 00:41:00,960
What if I'm more than that?

532
00:41:03,640 --> 00:41:06,960
What do you mean?
What are you trying to tell me?

533
00:41:07,560 --> 00:41:08,520
Nuch.

534
00:41:09,040 --> 00:41:12,760
Go upstairs and take care of your son.
Please. Don't start another fight.

535
00:41:18,680 --> 00:41:20,320
If you ask me…

536
00:41:22,240 --> 00:41:23,560
I'll do it.

537
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:26,600
-Hey.
-Mom, look at her.

538
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:27,760
Look at her with Raiwin.

539
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:30,120
-This has gone too far, Nuchwara.
-What?

540
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:32,400
I can't hold his hand?

541
00:41:33,200 --> 00:41:35,680
Then what part of Raiwin
would you rather I touch?

542
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:37,040
That's enough.

543
00:41:39,600 --> 00:41:40,800
What?

544
00:41:42,680 --> 00:41:45,120
-Enough. Stop.
-Stop.

545
00:41:47,680 --> 00:41:48,800
Enough.

546
00:41:51,720 --> 00:41:54,360
Aunt Ann, take Papang upstairs first.

547
00:41:54,440 --> 00:41:55,880
-Okay.
-Go. Quickly.

548
00:41:57,400 --> 00:41:58,240
-Stop.
-Ramil.

549
00:42:00,120 --> 00:42:01,720
-Enough. Stop.
-Chayanee.

550
00:42:03,960 --> 00:42:05,320
You too.

551
00:42:05,400 --> 00:42:07,160
You're protecting her.

552
00:42:07,240 --> 00:42:09,040
I'm not protecting her.

553
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:11,680
But you've gone too far.

554
00:42:11,760 --> 00:42:14,880
That video is already
being shared everywhere.

555
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:18,880
It damages my reputation too.
How am I supposed to govern people?

556
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:20,720
Then I'll go after

557
00:42:20,800 --> 00:42:23,480
-everyone who posted it.
-Enough.

558
00:42:23,560 --> 00:42:27,120
You never blame yourself.
You blame everyone else for everything.

559
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:31,560
You're yelling at me

560
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:34,240
when all of this happened because of her.

561
00:42:35,800 --> 00:42:40,040
If you hadn't asked me to let her stay,
I never would have kept her here.

562
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:45,240
Answer me.

563
00:42:46,760 --> 00:42:49,840
Why are you always protecting her?

564
00:42:50,520 --> 00:42:53,920
Is she Ramil's wife or yours?

565
00:42:56,720 --> 00:42:58,160
Answer me!

566
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:05,800
I said answer me.

567
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:11,240
If no one else is going to say it,

568
00:43:11,760 --> 00:43:14,520
-I will. The truth is, I'm--
-Nuch.

569
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:15,840
Chayanee.

570
00:43:20,320 --> 00:43:21,560
I'm moving back home.

571
00:43:26,040 --> 00:43:29,120
No. You have to stay here with me.

572
00:43:29,800 --> 00:43:31,640
If you never listen to me…

573
00:43:33,520 --> 00:43:34,680
then why are we together?

574
00:43:41,440 --> 00:43:42,600
All this time,

575
00:43:43,440 --> 00:43:46,800
I've given in and bent over
backwards for you,

576
00:43:48,440 --> 00:43:52,000
but you're just too self-centered.
You've never changed anything.

577
00:43:54,000 --> 00:43:56,200
I can't take it anymore.

578
00:43:57,560 --> 00:44:01,720
No. You can't leave me.

579
00:44:01,800 --> 00:44:03,160
We're done.

580
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:08,080
Raiwin, wait.

581
00:44:08,680 --> 00:44:12,800
You can't leave. You have to stay with me.
I'm not letting you go.

582
00:44:19,080 --> 00:44:21,720
-Let go.
-I won't let you go.

583
00:44:25,840 --> 00:44:28,600
Please don't leave me.

584
00:44:38,040 --> 00:44:39,400
Hey!

585
00:44:39,480 --> 00:44:43,720
I said come back. Don't leave me.

586
00:44:45,840 --> 00:44:47,040
Chayanee.

587
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:53,480
Chayanee.

588
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:59,040
-Miss Chayanee!
-Sweetheart.

589
00:44:59,120 --> 00:45:02,400
-My dear.
-Miss Chayanee.

590
00:45:02,480 --> 00:45:04,640
Take her to the hospital.

591
00:45:06,720 --> 00:45:08,960
Please help her.

592
00:45:10,240 --> 00:45:11,640
Get her to a doctor.

593
00:45:11,720 --> 00:45:15,280
Chayanee. Someone help.

594
00:45:15,360 --> 00:45:17,000
Oh, sweetheart.

595
00:45:23,400 --> 00:45:26,040
Don't get in my way.

596
00:45:26,120 --> 00:45:28,640
I need to get clothes for Miss Chayanee.

597
00:45:28,720 --> 00:45:30,600
She has to stay in the hospital.

598
00:45:32,960 --> 00:45:34,200
What a shame.

599
00:45:35,080 --> 00:45:37,080
I thought she had died.

600
00:45:50,920 --> 00:45:52,880
I don't understand you.

601
00:45:54,120 --> 00:45:55,960
You act sweet and caring toward Ramil,

602
00:45:56,040 --> 00:46:00,360
but you keep going after Raiwin too.
What exactly do you want?

603
00:46:00,960 --> 00:46:02,440
Where should we start?

604
00:46:03,880 --> 00:46:05,920
As for Raiwin,

605
00:46:07,360 --> 00:46:09,160
I won't ever get back with him.

606
00:46:10,080 --> 00:46:12,120
Then why do you keep going after him?

607
00:46:12,200 --> 00:46:15,920
I just want to get under Chayanee's skin.

608
00:46:16,000 --> 00:46:17,920
And I want revenge on Raiwin

609
00:46:18,600 --> 00:46:19,960
for hurting me.

610
00:46:21,960 --> 00:46:23,480
I just want him

611
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:26,000
to hurt even more than I did.

612
00:46:27,400 --> 00:46:29,880
Revenge isn't going to make you happy.

613
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:34,000
I'm willing to hurt.

614
00:46:35,880 --> 00:46:38,240
I have Ramil to heal my wounds.

615
00:46:39,440 --> 00:46:40,880
What do you mean?

616
00:46:41,600 --> 00:46:43,680
I think Ramil is a good man.

617
00:46:44,360 --> 00:46:46,080
Someone I can depend on.

618
00:46:47,760 --> 00:46:49,000
So,

619
00:46:49,840 --> 00:46:51,960
I want to build a life with him.

620
00:46:56,400 --> 00:46:58,840
I don't care whether
I'm crossing a line with you.

621
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:05,160
If it makes me happy and helps me survive…

622
00:47:06,560 --> 00:47:08,320
I'll fight all the way.

623
00:47:09,280 --> 00:47:10,400
For my son.

624
00:47:16,080 --> 00:47:17,960
Stop using your son as an excuse.

625
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:20,120
It's just for yourself.

626
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:43,480
So how is Chayanee?

627
00:47:44,400 --> 00:47:48,400
Aunt Chamoi said she has to stay in
the hospital, but it doesn't seem serious.

628
00:47:49,000 --> 00:47:53,520
Does Chayanee have any
existing medical condition?

629
00:47:53,600 --> 00:47:54,840
No.

630
00:47:55,640 --> 00:47:58,600
That's strange. She suddenly fainted.

631
00:47:59,920 --> 00:48:01,360
She must have been furious.

632
00:48:03,040 --> 00:48:04,200
Ramil.

633
00:48:04,800 --> 00:48:08,400
Why did you stop me earlier
when I tried to defend Nuchwara?

634
00:48:09,320 --> 00:48:14,560
I think it's finally time
we told the truth.

635
00:48:17,480 --> 00:48:20,840
But if Papang finds out,
he'll be shocked and heartbroken.

636
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:24,160
I'll try to explain it to him.

637
00:48:25,440 --> 00:48:26,560
Look.

638
00:48:27,600 --> 00:48:29,560
We've carried this secret long enough.

639
00:48:30,640 --> 00:48:34,640
Everyone has to take responsibility
for what they've done.

640
00:48:51,200 --> 00:48:52,440
Raiwin.

641
00:48:54,440 --> 00:48:56,240
Please don't leave me.

642
00:48:59,600 --> 00:49:02,720
Get some rest.
I'll come visit you again tomorrow.

643
00:49:07,680 --> 00:49:09,600
I'm pregnant.

644
00:49:14,080 --> 00:49:19,000
Raiwin, the doctor said Chayanee
is three months pregnant.

645
00:49:22,720 --> 00:49:24,960
I found out a while ago.

646
00:49:25,600 --> 00:49:29,360
I was going to surprise you with
the good news, but then this happened.

647
00:49:30,040 --> 00:49:32,120
You're going to be a father.

648
00:49:45,720 --> 00:49:49,320
If a dog barks at you, you don't
bark back. Otherwise, you're no better.

649
00:49:49,400 --> 00:49:52,760
I love you.
I want to spend my life with you.

650
00:49:52,840 --> 00:49:54,920
I'll scrub all the filth out.

651
00:49:55,000 --> 00:49:57,000
You have to throw her and her son out.

652
00:49:57,080 --> 00:49:58,600
Pong came back to see Liu?

653
00:49:58,680 --> 00:50:02,520
Then those two must be working together
on something terrible.

654
00:50:02,600 --> 00:50:04,320
‎NEXT EPISODE

655
00:50:04,400 --> 00:50:06,360
You were trying to make me lose my baby.

656
00:50:06,440 --> 00:50:08,720
Chayanee, don't!

657
00:50:08,800 --> 00:50:11,880
I was his first wife.

658
00:50:11,960 --> 00:50:16,160
I've been doing wrong for far too long.
I'm going to make things right.

659
00:52:08,400 --> 00:52:12,440
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
